+# Architectural Diagrams & Neural Training Assets
+
+This directory and associated directories contain diagrams and preliminary evaluation assets for neural network architectures developed within the WSmart+ Route framework:
+
+- **Architecture diagrams (`Images/Architectures/`, 9 files):**
+  - `AM-Architecture.pdf`: Standard Attention Model (Kool et al., 2019) encoder-decoder architecture.
+  - `Attention-Block.pdf`: Multi-Head Attention and Feed-Forward sublayer structure.
+  - `DDAM-Architecture.pdf`: Deep Decoder Attention Model architecture.
+  - `Deep-Decoder.png`: High-resolution render of the deep decoder stack.
+  - `AMGC-Architecture.pdf`: Attention Model with Graph Convolutional layers.
+  - `AGC-Block.pdf`: Adaptive Graph Convolution sublayer component.
+  - `TransGCN-Architecture.pdf`: Transformer + Graph Convolutional Network hybrid architecture.
+  - `GraphConv-Block.pdf`: Graph convolutional layer block diagram.
+  - `All-Blocks.pdf`: Composite diagram of modular network layers.
+
+- **Preliminary neural training and comparison plots (5 files):**
+  - `Images/Results/Training/am_cost20.png`: Cost trajectory during synthetic 20-node training.
+  - `Images/Results/Training/am_loss20.png`: Actor loss curve during synthetic 20-node training.
+  - `Images/Results/am_comp.png`: Efficiency comparison across 20-node Attention Model variants.
+  - `Images/Results/comp_temp_op20.png`: Temperature and sampling comparison across instances.
+  - `Images/next_models.png`: Conceptual roadmap of planned neural routing models.
+
+## Exclusion Rationale (Owner Ruling Q15)
+
+In accordance with project steering ruling **Q15**, these 14 assets are excluded from `paper.tex`. The current paper focuses strictly on establishing empirical baselines across classical exact and heuristic constructors on real municipal waste collection networks. These neural architecture diagrams and preliminary synthetic training plots are preserved here for a subsequent journal publication dedicated to neural combinatorial optimization and multi-scale routing architectures.
